all-transcripts/2019/02/21/aptargroup-atr-q4-2018-earnings-conference-call-tr.aspx"},{"c":"ATR 2018 Q4","e":"atr","d":"2019-02-21","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Bob Kuhn","x":"We did pass-throughs in the quarter, which positively impacted the top line by between that and general price increase about 1.5%.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/02/21/aptargroup-atr-q4-2018-earnings-conference-call-tr.aspx"},{"c":"ATR 2018 Q4","e":"atr","d":"2019-02-21","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Bob Kuhn","x":"The primary reasons for the decrease in cash flow relate to $64 million of cash outflows related to our restructuring and acquisition costs and higher capital expenditures compared to the prior year, primarily related to our business transformation.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/02/21/aptargroup-atr-q4-2018-earnings-conference-call-tr.aspx"},{"c":"ATR 2018 Q4","e":"atr","d":"2019-02-21","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Stephan Tanda","x":"We also finished the year with a strong EBITDA improvement when we exclude costs related to our acquisitions and restructuring initiatives.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/02/21/aptargroup-atr-q4-2018-earnings-conference-call-tr.aspx"},{"c":"ATR 2019 Q1","e":"atr","d":"2019-05-01","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Stephan B. Tanda","x":"So with a depending on the contract anywhere between 60 to 90 days lag we pass it on.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/05/01/aptargroup-inc-atr-q1-2019-earnings-call-transcrip.aspx"},{"c":"ATR 2019 Q1","e":"atr","d":"2019-05-01","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Stephan B. Tanda","x":"…we now is really in improving operations and then year three, it's about Frank the footprint reducing headcount and G&A, especially in Europe and North America. The target is to achieve the 80 million improvements run rate by the end of 2020 and be comfortably in our long-term targets, which","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/05/01/aptargroup-inc-atr-q1-2019-earnings-call-transcrip.aspx"},{"c":"ATR 2019 Q1","e":"atr","d":"2019-05-01","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Stephan B. Tanda","x":"And then lastly, the headcount reductions in G&A improvements, they are fully mapped out, there actually being discussed with stakeholders in the respective countries.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/05/01/aptargroup-inc-atr-q1-2019-earnings-call-transcrip.aspx"},{"c":"ATR 2019 Q2","e":"atr","d":"2019-08-01","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Adam Josephson","x":"And one on restructuring for either Stephan or Bob.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/01/aptargroup-inc-atr-q2-2019-earnings-call-transcrip.aspx"},{"c":"ATR 2019 Q2","e":"atr","d":"2019-08-01","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Adam Josephson","x":"So I am just wondering if the restructuring program is as you expect it to be or Beauty and Home has been just more difficult than you imagined it would be, such that the $80 million of savings will be more difficult to come by then, perhaps you thought when you announced the program?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/01/aptargroup-inc-atr-q2-2019-earnings-call-transcrip.aspx"},{"c":"ATR 2019 Q3","e":"atr","d":"2019-11-01","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Stephan B. Tanda","x":"We also are passing through lower resin costs to our customers, creating an additional headwind on Food & Beverage's top line.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/11/01/aptargroup-inc-atr-q3-2019-earnings-call-transcrip.aspx"},{"c":"ATR 2019 Q3","e":"atr","d":"2019-11-01","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Stephan B. Tanda","x":"And then the third one is headcount reduction and SG&A streamlining, also corporate support functions that is quite a bit also in Europe, including the installation of the shared service center, which requires all work channels of improvement approved -- approval also in France, and that is a…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/11/01/aptargroup-inc-atr-q3-2019-earnings-call-transcrip.aspx"},{"c":"ATR 2019 Q3","e":"atr","d":"2019-11-01","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Stephan B. Tanda","x":"Now we are also looking at scenarios to further streamline our footprint.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/11/01/aptargroup-inc-atr-q3-2019-earnings-call-transcrip.aspx"},{"c":"ATR 2019 Q4","e":"atr","d":"2020-02-21","l":"tariffs","r":"analyst","s":"Adam Josephson","x":"And if we look at the last couple of years, China slowed down and that was before the trade war.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/21/aptargroup-inc-atr-q4-2019-earnings-call-transcrip.aspx"},{"c":"ATR 2019 Q4","e":"atr","d":"2020-02-21","l":"tariffs","r":"analyst","s":"Adam Josephson","x":"And now obviously there's the trade war and now there's coronavirus.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/21/aptargroup-inc-atr-q4-2019-earnings-call-transcrip.aspx"},{"c":"ATR 2019 Q4","e":"atr","d":"2020-02-21","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Bob Kuhn","x":"For the fourth quarter of 2019 reported sales declined 2%, and core sales declined 1%, in part due to the passing through of lower resin costs to our customers.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/21/aptargroup-inc-atr-q4-2019-earnings-call-transcrip.aspx"},{"c":"ATR 2019 Q4","e":"atr","d":"2020-02-21","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Bob Kuhn","x":"So on the resin side, again, it depends on where we are in that cycle of pass-through.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/21/aptargroup-inc-atr-q4-2019-earnings-call-transcrip.aspx"},{"c":"ATR 2019 Q4","e":"atr","d":"2020-02-21","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Stephan B. Tanda","x":"This is a continuation of other steps we have taken to streamline and modernize our Beauty and Home footprint.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/21/aptargroup-inc-atr-q4-2019-earnings-call-transcrip.aspx"},{"c":"ATR 2019 Q4","e":"atr","d":"2020-02-21","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Bob Kuhn","x":"Higher earnings due to less restructuring and acquisition costs and working capital improvements led to the increase in free cash flow.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/21/aptargroup-inc-atr-q4-2019-earnings-call-transcrip.aspx"},{"c":"ATR 2020 Q1","e":"atr","d":"2020-05-01","l":"theater","r":"management","s":"Bob Kuhn","x":"Even with the lifting of the restriction state by state, it's going to be a question of how comfortable people are going to be going back to the movie theaters, how comfortable are they going to be going into shopping malls and small stores and things like that.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/01/aptargroup-inc-atr-q1-2020-earnings-call-transcrip.aspx"},{"c":"ATR 2020 Q1","e":"atr","d":"2020-05-01","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Bob Kuhn","x":"Core sales decreased 2% in the quarter primarily due to the passing through of lower resin prices to our customers, which accounted for approximately 5% of negative growth on the top line.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/01/aptargroup-inc-atr-q1-2020-earnings-call-transcrip.aspx"},{"c":"ATR 2020 Q1","e":"atr","d":"2020-05-01","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Bob Kuhn","x":"We are also passing through price adjustments to our customers.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/01/aptargroup-inc-atr-q1-2020-earnings-call-transcrip.aspx"},{"c":"ATR 2020 Q2","e":"atr","d":"2020-07-31","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Stephan Tanda","x":"So we're also passing on some of that with price increases in the injectable space, and I think we did a few percentage in quarter two already.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/07/31/aptargroup-inc-atr-q2-2020-earnings-call-transcrip.aspx"},{"c":"ATR 2020 Q2","e":"atr","d":"2020-07-31","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Bob Kuhn","x":"…for the follow-on, George, because I did want to mention that the opposite of that decremental comment that I made is that when it does come back, the volume to, I would say, above that line, I think what we've done is we've done a tremendous amount of cost savings throughout the transformation.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/07/31/aptargroup-inc-atr-q2-2020-earnings-call-transcrip.aspx"},{"c":"ATR 2020 Q2","e":"atr","d":"2020-07-31","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Stephan Tanda","x":"We've done a lot of good work in taking cost out and preparing for the upturn.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/07/31/aptargroup-inc-atr-q2-2020-earnings-call-transcrip.aspx"},{"c":"ATR 2020 Q3","e":"atr","d":"2020-10-30","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Stephan Tanda","x":"In addition, the effects of passing through lower resin prices to customers also affected the segment's overall growth.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/10/30/aptargroup-inc-atr-q3-2020-earnings-call-transcrip/"},{"c":"ATR 2020 Q3","e":"atr","d":"2020-10-30","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Bob Kuhn","x":"You had a little bit of a positive on the Beauty + Home side, on the EBITDA side due to the pass-through, and that was more or less on a consolidated basis, offset by negative on the EBITDA flow-through side, Food + Beverage.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/10/30/aptargroup-inc-atr-q3-2020-earnings-call-transcrip/"},{"c":"ATR 2020 Q3","e":"atr","d":"2020-10-30","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Stephan Tanda","x":"We also continue to implement cost containment measures and streamline our footprint.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/10/30/aptargroup-inc-atr-q3-2020-earnings-call-transcrip/"},{"c":"ATR 2020 Q3","e":"atr","d":"2020-10-30","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Bob Kuhn","x":"We are continuing to rightsize our footprint and have recently announced facility closures in Ireland and Spain.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/10/30/aptargroup-inc-atr-q3-2020-earnings-call-transcrip/"},{"c":"ATR 2020 Q4","e":"atr","d":"2021-02-19","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Bob Kuhn","x":"Turning to our Food & Beverage segment, core sales increased 13% despite resin pass through headwinds of 2%.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/19/aptargroup-inc-atr-q4-2020-earnings-call-transcrip/"},{"c":"ATR 2020 Q4","e":"atr","d":"2021-02-19","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Bob Kuhn","x":"I don't have right at my fingertips exactly what each segment is doing because it's really depending on the pass-through, the volumes in the quarter, which customers.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/19/aptargroup-inc-atr-q4-2020-earnings-call-transcrip/"},{"c":"ATR 2020 Q4","e":"atr","d":"2021-02-19","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Bob Kuhn","x":"So, if you look at the China and the French decorating facility, those are as much, I would say, efficiency, cost savings type of plant consolidations.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/19/aptargroup-inc-atr-q4-2020-earnings-call-transcrip/"},{"c":"ATR 2021 Q1","e":"atr","d":"2021-04-30","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Stephan Tanda","x":"Price increases also contributed to our top line growth that we are passing on increased resin costs to our customers.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/04/30/aptargroup-inc-atr-q1-2021-earnings-call-transcrip/"},{"c":"ATR 2021 Q1","e":"atr","d":"2021-04-30","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Stephan Tanda","x":"We are also maintaining initiatives to contain costs and manage inflation that includes raising prices to offset increases in raw material and other costs, while investing in key growth areas including adding capacity to supply the beauty market in China.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/04/30/aptargroup-inc-atr-q1-2021-earnings-call-transcrip/"},{"c":"ATR 2021 Q1","e":"atr","d":"2021-04-30","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Bob Kuhn","x":"First quarter adjusted earnings per share excluding restructuring expenses, and the gain on the equity investment increased 10% to $1.09 per share on a comparable basis with the prior year, including adjusting for currency effects.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/04/30/aptargroup-inc-atr-q1-2021-earnings-call-transcrip/"},{"c":"ATR 2021 Q1","e":"atr","d":"2021-04-30","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Bob Kuhn","x":"We expect a second quarter adjusted earnings per share, excluding restructuring and any change in the fair value of equity investments to be in the range of $0.91 to $0.99 per share.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/04/30/aptargroup-inc-atr-q1-2021-earnings-call-transcrip/"},{"c":"ATR 2021 Q2","e":"atr","d":"2021-07-30","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Stephan Tanda","x":"In our Food + Beverage segment, top line growth was strong across each market segment with about 60% of the growth coming from price adjustments related to the passing through of higher resin costs.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/30/aptargroup-inc-atr-q2-2021-earnings-call-transcrip/"},{"c":"ATR 2021 Q2","e":"atr","d":"2021-07-30","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Stephan Tanda","x":"It continues to be a very challenging input cost environment, and we are in the process of passing through higher input costs to our customers.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/30/aptargroup-inc-atr-q2-2021-earnings-call-transcrip/"},{"c":"ATR 2021 Q2","e":"atr","d":"2021-07-30","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Bob Kuhn","x":"We expect our third quarter adjusted earnings per share, excluding any restructuring expenses, acquisition costs and changes in the fair value of equity investments, to be in the range of $0.90 to $0.98 per share.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/30/aptargroup-inc-atr-q2-2021-earnings-call-transcrip/"},{"c":"ATR 2021 Q3","e":"atr","d":"2021-10-29","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Stephan B. Tanda","x":"Our Beauty + Home and Food + Beverage margins reflected the rapidly accelerating inflationary environment and related pass-through effects as well as supply chain challenges.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/10/29/aptargroup-inc-atr-q3-2021-earnings-call-transcrip/"},{"c":"ATR 2021 Q3","e":"atr","d":"2021-10-29","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Stephan B. Tanda","x":"As a reminder, the passing through of increased input cost on a dollar-for-dollar basis has the effect of compressing margin percentages.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/10/29/aptargroup-inc-atr-q3-2021-earnings-call-transcrip/"},{"c":"ATR 2021 Q3","e":"atr","d":"2021-10-29","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Robert W. Kuhn","x":"We expect our fourth quarter adjusted earnings per share, excluding any restructuring expenses, acquisition costs and changes in the unrealized fair value of equity investments, to be in the range of $0.88 to $0.96 per share.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/10/29/aptargroup-inc-atr-q3-2021-earnings-call-transcrip/"},{"c":"ATR 2021 Q3","e":"atr","d":"2021-10-29","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Robert W. Kuhn","x":"As far as the larger-than-expected restructuring costs, we had talked about even last year shutting down some of our East Coast operations and merging them into existing North American facilities.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/10/29/aptargroup-inc-atr-q3-2021-earnings-call-transcrip/"},{"c":"ATR 2025 Q2","e":"atr","d":"2025-08-01","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Vanessa Kanu","x":"…beauty segment by market, fragrance, facial skincare, and color cosmetics core sales decreased 4% primarily due to lower sales of skincare dispensing products for indie brands as well as muted customer demand for our prestige fragrance dispensing technologies, given tariff-related uncertainties.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/08/05/aptargroup-atr-q2-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"ATR 2025 Q2","e":"atr","d":"2025-08-01","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Stephan Tanda","x":"In the second quarter, we saw some end market pull forward order volumes from quarter three to avoid tariff uncertainties, as customers move to secure inventory ahead of potential trade disruptions.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/08/05/aptargroup-atr-q2-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"ATR 2025 Q2","e":"atr","d":"2025-08-01","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Vanessa Kanu","x":"At the total company level, due to ongoing cost reduction efforts, increased volumes, and improved revenue mix, consolidated gross margins expanded over 30 basis points in Q2 year over year, while SG&A as a percentage of sales declined from 16.4% last year to 15.6% this year, an 80 basis point…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/08/05/aptargroup-atr-q2-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"ATR 2025 Q2","e":"atr","d":"2025-08-01","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Vanessa Kanu","x":"We anticipate third quarter adjusted earnings per share, which excludes any restructuring expenses, acquisition costs, changes in the unrealized fair value of equity investments, as well as an anticipated revaluation of our B2I investments, to be in the range of $1.53 to $1.61 per share.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/08/05/aptargroup-atr-q2-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"ATR 2026 Q1","e":"atr","d":"2026-05-01","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Vanessa Kanu","x":"While volumes were up, core sales were impacted by the pass-through of lower resin pricing.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/01/aptargroup-atr-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"ATR 2026 Q1","e":"atr","d":"2026-05-01","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Vanessa Kanu","x":"As a reminder, as costs are passed through, margin percentage will experience some compression.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/01/aptargroup-atr-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"ATR 2026 Q2","e":"atr","d":"2026-07-31","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Vanessa Kanu","x":"And, Ghansham, I can absolutely confirm to you that there is no P&L benefit in the quarter from tariff refunds.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/07/aptar-atr-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"ATR 2026 Q2","e":"atr","d":"2026-07-31","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Vanessa Kanu","x":"None of it was tariff refunds or anything else of that nature, of a 1-time nature.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/07/aptar-atr-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"ATR 2026 Q2","e":"atr","d":"2026-07-31","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Vanessa Kanu","x":"As demand for beauty dispensing systems and the pass through of higher input costs more than compensated for lower tooling sales.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/07/aptar-atr-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"ATR 2026 Q2","e":"atr","d":"2026-07-31","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Vanessa Kanu","x":"Compared to the prior year Strong volume growth particularly in beverages, and the pass through of higher input costs more than compensated for lower tooling sales.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/07/aptar-atr-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"ATR 2026 Q3","e":"atr","d":"2026-10